CORE
main.go
--go-race-check --unwind 4
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[go::main\.main\.data-race\.\d+\] line 11 data race \(write\): FAILURE$
^\[go::main\.main\$lit1\.data-race\.\d+\] line 8 data race \(read\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
Repeating symbolic execution
shadow memory does not resolve the accessed object: FAILURE
^warning: ignoring
--
The goroutine's insertion sets flags in the shadow memory of the map's
header, which has the header's type: the flag values written into its
`keys` pointer must not count as values of a shared pointer, which made
symbolic execution repeat, with the goroutine seeing the keys array that it
allocates only later.
